			(property "Datasheet" "https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/max17048-max17049.pdf"
				(at 0 -11.43 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
			(property "Description" "Maxim/Analog Devices MAX17048 micropower 1-cell Li+ ModelGauge fuel gauge IC, I2C interface, 8-pin TDFN-EP (2x2mm, package code T822+3, ordering part MAX17048G+T10). Pin/Bump numbers and functions verified directly against the real Maxim datasheet 19-6171 Rev 2 (8/12), page 6 'Pin/Bump Configurations' and 'Pin/Bump Descriptions' table: 1=CTG (connect to ground), 2=CELL (not internally connected on the single-cell MAX17048 -- only used on the dual-cell MAX17049), 3=VDD (power input AND the actual cell-voltage sense input for MAX17048, connect to positive battery terminal), 4=GND, 5=ALRT (open-drain active-low alert), 6=QSTRT (quick-start input, tie to GND if unused), 7=SCL, 8=SDA (open-drain I2C data), EP=exposed pad, connect to GND (TDFN only -- no EP on the alternative 8-bump WLP option, package code W80B1+1, which this project does NOT use because 0.9x1.7mm WLP is impractical to hand-solder/rework). Chose the TDFN-EP variant (MAX17048G+T10) over the WLP variant (MAX17048X+T10) specifically for hand-assembly/rework feasibility on a bench-built bay station. Also confirmed the MAX17048 (1-cell) vs MAX17049 (2-cell) part-number distinction directly from the datasheet -- this design uses a single Li-ion cell so MAX17048 is correct."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
